---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BlogPostHeader from '../../components/BlogPostHeader.astro';
import { currentMonthYear } from '../../utils/site-date';

const title = "What Response Can You Expect From Your Airport PCN Appeal? | AppealAirportPCN";
const description = "A plain-English guide to common replies after a parking appeal, what a cancellation or rejection means, and how to check your next steps.";
const canonical = "https://appealairportpcn.co.uk/blog/what-responses-to-expect/";

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": "What responses to expect when you appeal an airport parking charge",
  "description": description,
  "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "AppealAirportPCN" },
  "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "AppealAirportPCN.co.uk" },
  "datePublished": "2026-04-15",
  "dateModified": "2026-10-05"
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} schema={schema}>
  <BlogPostHeader title="What responses to expect when you appeal an airport parking charge" breadcrumbLabel="What responses to expect" breadcrumbHref="/blog/what-responses-to-expect/" updatedDate={currentMonthYear.toUpperCase()} />
  <main>
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="blog-post">
        <p>What might a parking company say after you appeal? Here are common replies and what you can do next. The exact wording and process vary by operator.</p>

        <h2>1. The company cancels the charge</h2>
        <p>The reply may simply say the notice has been cancelled and no further action is needed.</p>
        <p><strong>What to do:</strong> Keep the cancellation letter or email. If it confirms the charge is cancelled, no further appeal is needed.</p>

        <h2>2. The company cancels but defends its signs</h2>
        <p>A company may cancel the charge but also say it believes its signs and terms were clear. The tone does not change the fact that it has cancelled this notice.</p>
        <div class="callout">
          <strong>Key point:</strong> Read the whole letter and check that it clearly confirms cancellation and says no further payment is due. Keep a copy for your records.
        </div>

        <h2>3. The company rejects your appeal</h2>
        <p>A rejection is not necessarily the end. Read the reasons and check whether your letter includes details of a second-stage appeal. If the operator is a BPA member, it may provide a POPLA code. Our guide explains <a href="/blog/what-is-popla/">how to make a POPLA appeal</a>.</p>
        <p>Use the deadline and instructions in the rejection letter. You can also read about <a href="/blog/what-is-pofa-and-why-it-matters/">POFA</a>, <a href="/blog/bpa-code-of-practice-signage/">signage</a> and the <a href="/blog/five-minute-consideration-period/">five-minute consideration period</a> when deciding what points apply to your case.</p>

        <h2>4. You do not get a reply</h2>
        <p>Check the operator's code of practice and the instructions on your notice. The BPA Code sets response requirements for its members, but not receiving a reply does not automatically give you a POPLA code. Contact the operator in writing, keep a copy, and ask how to proceed if the deadline in the code has passed.</p>

        <div class="disclaimer">
          <strong>Disclaimer:</strong> This article is for information only and does not constitute legal advice. Response wording varies by operator. For complex cases, consult a solicitor or Citizens Advice.
        </div>

        <h2>Sources</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>POPLA, "Parking charges: understanding grace periods and appeal deadlines" (appeal to the operator within 28 days; POPLA within 28 days of rejection; ten-digit code; do not pay first). <strong>Primary.</strong> <a href="https://www.popla.co.uk/news/parking-charges-understanding-grace-periods-and-appeal-deadlines" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">POPLA</a></li>
          <li>POPLA FAQs (code from the operator on request if you appealed within 28 days). <strong>Primary.</strong> <a href="https://popla.co.uk/faqs" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">POPLA FAQs</a></li>
          <li>POPLA home page (if you delay payment after losing, the operator may add charges or use debt collection). <strong>Primary.</strong> <a href="https://popla.co.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">POPLA</a></li>
        </ol>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
